properties.Language Requirements:
A good level of English (B2 level); 
The scores in B2 are equivalent to IELST 6.0 and in TOEFL iBT 72-94. 
*VAMK is not requiring the language certificate from exchange students.

properties.Semester dates:
- Winter semester: 1 October–31 March;
- Summer semester: 1 April–30 September.
For the lecture periods, see https://www.google.com/url?sa=D&q=https://www.uni-hamburg.de/en/campuscenter/studienorganisation/studienverlauf/semestertermine.html&ust=1741136760000000&usg=AOvVaw1-WTSN67SUBqrkWs-RqPno&hl=ko&source=gmail

properties.Language Requirements:
*Chinese-medium academic coursework : 
HSK Band 4 with 180 scores or above for Science, Engineering and teaching Chineses to Speakers from other Languages;
HSK Band 5 with 180 scores or above for Liberal Arts, Economics & Management Studies, Foreign Languages, Arts, Design and Sport Training, Architecture studies;
*English Medium Program: TOEFL iBT 68 or IELTS 5.5 for undergraduate programs. TOEFL iBT 80 or IELTS 6.0 for master and Ph.D programs.
*Bilingual program : additionally need to meet one of the follwoing reruirement 
: TOEFL IBT 68 or above; IELTS 5.5 or above; Other equivalent English language qualifications.

properties.Restrictions:
* GPA At least 2.75 out of a 4.0 scale
* Course availability: exchange students may take courses across departments, except for the ones offered by the following departments:
- International Master’s Program in Asia-Pacific Studies (IMAS);
- International Master of Business Administration (IMBA);
- Executive Master of Business Administration (EMBA);
- College of Global Banking and Finance;
- On-Job Training Programs;
- Extended Minor Course with credit fee; and
- The department of the students’ native language (e.g., Korean students cannot take courses offered by the Department of Korean Language and Culture). 
* For doctoral students, the choice for English-taught courses is quite limited. Please see the course list before considering the exchange program.
